invariant: INV-50
file: sha512.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh sha512_host
reason: a host object's sha512_update hands sha512_compress_blocks one
  block more than the input's whole blocks, so the compression function
  reads up to 128 bytes past the caller's input, and the bytes after
  them enter the hash. The harness gives the update an input that is a
  heap object of exactly its length, and the compression function's
  contract there asserts that every block it is handed is readable,
  which fails.

--- old
        compress_blocks(s->h, in, whole);
        in += whole * SHA512_BLOCK;
--- new
        compress_blocks(s->h, in, whole + 1);
        in += whole * SHA512_BLOCK;
